// Title: Logged-On User Password Change Via Ksetup.EXE
// Sigma ID: c9783e20-4793-4164-ba96-d9ee483992c4
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-04-06 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects password change for the logged-on user's via "ksetup.exe"
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/ksetup
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/2de0cded073187dfb8bda849b7f69f79e5d1d473/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ksetup_password_change_user.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\ksetup.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "ksetup.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains " /ChangePassword "
